        "id": 150654,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-11-24T14:02:04.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>You can throw any Ennead Villain into a Vengeance format fight, just remove Shrine of the Ennead, Taste of Immortality (2), and Rise to Power (2). &nbsp;Treat (H) as 3 no matter the number of heroes.</p><p>The Ennead cards tell the highest, lowest HP Villains to act, so the Ennead Character acts as a support style character. &nbsp;It can be nasty, worst we had was Elemental Storm when Fright Train at +2 damage was almost dead. &nbsp;9 damage to all hero targets hurt.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I know this isn't what you are posting about, but it really works well.</p>",
